From 70e931c38b33a42b4d6a3946f2cac1bc018fb883 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ozark <ozark@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:43:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Wireless AA: phones no longer get stuck on "Connecting to
 Android Auto"

Two ways a phone waited forever:

- The Bluetooth handshake took each read as exactly one message. RFCOMM
  can deliver two messages in one read, or one in two; the extra or partial
  message was lost and the phone never got its answer. Messages are now
  framed by their length, and each phone has its own socket and buffer (a
  second phone, or the same one reconnecting, took over the first's socket).

- A phone that came back over Wi-Fi while its old session hadn't timed out
  yet was turned away, and port 5000 then stopped listening for good. A new
  wireless connection now replaces the old wireless session, the port keeps
  listening during a session, and a failed accept listens again.
